---
import Docs from "~/layouts/Docs.astro";
import cliPackage from "../../../../cli/package.json";
import { softwareApplicationSchema } from "~/lib/structured-data";
import { PUBLISHED_VERSION } from "~/lib/site-facts.generated";
---

<Docs
  title="Capabilities and install"
  description="Install Ashlr Stack for CLI or MCP use, inspect supported services, and understand source versions, credentials and provider costs."
  eyebrow="Getting started"
  extraSchemas={[softwareApplicationSchema()]}
>
  <h2 id="capabilities">What Stack can do</h2>
  <p>
    Stack is a pre-alpha CLI and stdio MCP bridge for planning and configuring
    supported project services on macOS, Linux and Windows. The MIT-licensed
    software is free; provider accounts, infrastructure and API usage can cost money.
    This documentation describes source version <strong>{cliPackage.version}</strong>.
    Source version and registry publication are separate.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>stack providers</code> lists the installed provider catalog.</li>
    <li><code>stack recommend "project brief"</code> ranks service choices.</li>
    <li><code>stack scan --json</code> inspects a local repository without provisioning.</li>
    <li><code>stack add &lt;provider&gt;</code> runs provider-specific setup.</li>
    <li><code>stack doctor</code> reports configured-service health.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="install">Install the CLI</h2>
  <p>
    The published 0.3.1 CLI and MCP packages declare Node.js 20 or newer, including
    when started through npx. The recorded public version is {PUBLISHED_VERSION};
    check other versions’ manifests and installed help before relying on a command.
    A source checkout uses <a href="https://bun.sh">Bun</a> for development.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`npm view @ashlr/stack version
npm i -g @ashlr/stack@${PUBLISHED_VERSION} ashlr-stack-mcp@${PUBLISHED_VERSION}
stack --version
stack --help
stack providers`}</code></pre>
  <p>For the current source checkout:</p>
  <pre><code>{`git clone https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-stack
cd ashlr-stack
bun install
bun run packages/cli/src/index.ts --help`}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="mcp">Connect an MCP client</h2>
  <p>
    Add this stdio server to your client's MCP configuration. Both packages are
    needed: the server forwards tool calls to the CLI. Run it in the intended
    project directory and inspect tool errors and output.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{JSON.stringify({ mcpServers: { "ashlr-stack": { command: "npx", args: ["-y", "-p", "@ashlr/stack", "-p", "ashlr-stack-mcp", "ashlr-stack-mcp"] } } }, null, 2)}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="boundaries">Credentials and limits</h2>
  <p>
    Authentication and provisioning vary by adapter. Vercel requires an existing
    personal access token. Selected credentials persist through
    <a href="https://phm.dev/secrets">Phantom Secrets</a>; setup processes and
    provider requests still handle values. MCP output is not a sandbox or a
    universal redaction boundary. Local removal does not delete remote resources.
    Review provider costs and authorize provisioning before running setup.
  </p>

  <h2 id="references">References for agents</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/cli">CLI reference</a> and <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP reference</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/for-ai-agents">Agent integration guide</a></li>
    <li><a href="/llms.txt">Generated documentation index</a> and <a href="/llms-full.txt">full text reference</a></li>
    <li><a href="/mcp.json">Machine-readable tool catalog</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-stack">Source repository</a> and <a href="https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-stack/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a></li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
